    <p class="eyebrow">About ARIES</p>
    <h1 data-split data-split-delay="120">A research hub built on evidence, not assumption</h1>
    <p class="lede">ARIES is the research hub of Amaze Consortium, dedicated to conducting
    structured grassroots research across Bangladesh and beyond, focused on understanding
    real-world data across multiple fields and domains.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--paper">
  <div class="container grid-split">
    <div class="prose" data-reveal="up">
    <p>
    It aims to move beyond assumptions and surface-level interpretations by gathering
    direct insights from individuals, communities, and institutions. Through systematic
    data collection and analysis, ARIES explores patterns in behaviour, perception,
    systems, and societal gaps that are often overlooked in conventional studies.</p>
    <p>
    ARIES is designed to function as a bridge between raw information and practical
    action. Its goal is not only to study problems but to transform findings into
    meaningful, evidence-based initiatives that can be implemented within and beyond
    the Consortium, combining qualitative and quantitative approaches so that
    insights reflect real conditions rather than theoretical assumptions.</p>
    <p>
    It also serves a second, deliberate purpose. Building and running each study is
    how ARIES itself grows: every pilot forms the foundation of a standing Amaze
    Researcher Team, and every finding is designed to feed directly back into an
    <em>insight-to-action</em> model, where a gap such as low critical-thinking
    scores among students becomes the brief for a concrete Amaze initiative, like a
    workshop or essay competition, rather than a statistic that sits on a shelf.</p>
    </div>

